      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The first reported case of a patient with left internal mammary artery bypass graft dissection secondary to selective coronary and graft arteriography is presented. The intimal tear and false lumen could not be seen with flouroscopy during catheterization. This later led to antero-septal myocardial infarction."},
